WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.665 --> 00:00:03.490
Guadarfía and the Island of San Borondón

2
00:00:04.365 --> 00:00:10.005
When boats travelled under sail and maps
were drawn on parchment, Guadarfía was an

3
00:00:10.005 --> 00:00:12.510
apprentice sailor on a small ship.

4
00:00:13.085 --> 00:00:17.525
One afternoon, the ship was crossing the
sea near the island we now call

5
00:00:17.525 --> 00:00:18.525
La Graciosa.

6
00:00:19.205 --> 00:00:22.390
An unknown land appeared behind the band
of mist.

7
00:00:23.125 --> 00:00:27.005
It had a dark mountain, trees and a
gleaming beach.

8
00:00:27.005 --> 00:00:33.885
The captain remembered the stories of San
Borondón, the island that appeared and

9
00:00:33.885 --> 00:00:34.885
disappeared.

10
00:00:35.325 --> 00:00:42.145
Guadarfía pointed to the horizon and said:
“Island of mist, you appear and then you

11
00:00:42.145 --> 00:00:43.145
disappear.”

12
00:00:43.685 --> 00:00:49.605
The crew changed course, but the further
the ship sailed, the further away the

13
00:00:49.605 --> 00:00:57.690
island seemed. Then a fog came in so thick
that they had to lower the sails and wait.

14
00:00:58.645 --> 00:01:00.930
By dawn, the mist had gone.

15
00:01:01.645 --> 00:01:04.990
There was only sea in front of the ship.

16
00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:10.545
The captain marked the spot on his chart,
and Guadarfía drew the shape he

17
00:01:10.545 --> 00:01:11.545
remembered.

18
00:01:12.025 --> 00:01:17.410
Other sailors told of similar sights, and
some maps included San Borondón.

19
00:01:17.725 --> 00:01:19.810
Yet no one managed to reach it.

20
00:01:20.625 --> 00:01:27.430
The island kept appearing in stories,
always behind the mist: “Island of mist,

21
00:01:27.845 --> 00:01:30.570
you appear and then you disappear.”

